7.Handling Missing Data
In df, replace all NaN values in column 'B' with the mean of column 'B'.

df = pd.DataFrame({'A': [1, 2, np.nan], 'B': [np.nan, 5, 6]})
(Write the code)
code:
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

# Create the DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame({
    'A': [1, 2, np.nan],
    'B': [np.nan, 5, 6]
})

# Calculate the mean of column 'B'
mean_B = df['B'].mean()

# Fill missing values in column 'B' with the mean
df['B'] = df['B'].fillna(mean_B)

# Show the result
print(df)
8.GroupBy & Aggregation
Group df by 'Region', then compute the sum of 'Sales' and mean of 'Profit' for each group. Reset the index.

df = pd.DataFrame({
    'Region': ['North', 'South', 'North', 'South'],
    'Sales': [100, 200, 150, 250],
    'Profit': [20, 30, 25, 40]
})
(Write the code)
code:
----
import pandas as pd

# Create the DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame({
    'Region': ['North', 'South', 'North', 'South'],
    'Sales': [100, 200, 150, 250],
    'Profit': [20, 30, 25, 40]
})

# Group by 'Region' and calculate sum of 'Sales' and mean of 'Profit'
result = df.groupby('Region').agg({
    'Sales': 'sum',
    'Profit': 'mean'
}).reset_index()

# Show the result
print(result)
9.Merging DataFrames
Merge orders and customers on 'cust_id', keeping all orders (even if no customer match exists).

orders = pd.DataFrame({'order_id': [1, 2], 'cust_id': [101, 102]})
customers = pd.DataFrame({'cust_id': [101, 103], 'name': ['Alice', 'Bob']})
(Write the code)

code:
---
import pandas as pd

# Create the DataFrames
orders = pd.DataFrame({'order_id': [1, 2], 'cust_id': [101, 102]})
customers = pd.DataFrame({'cust_id': [101, 103], 'name': ['Alice', 'Bob']})

# Merge orders with customers using a left join
result = pd.merge(orders, customers, on='cust_id', how='left')

# Show the result
print(result)
10.Time Series & Resampling
Convert 'Date' to datetime, set it as the index, and resample to monthly frequency, summing 'Value'.

df = pd.DataFrame({
    'Date': ['2023-01-05', '2023-01-15', '2023-02-10'],
    'Value': [10, 20, 30]
})
(Write the code)
import pandas as pd

# Create the DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame({
    'Date': ['2023-01-05', '2023-01-15', '2023-02-10'],
    'Value': [10, 20, 30]
})

# Convert 'Date' to datetime type
df['Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Date'])

# Set 'Date' as the index
df.set_index('Date', inplace=True)

# Resample to monthly frequency and sum the 'Value'
monthly_sum = df.resample('M').sum()

print(monthly_sum)



